hello welcome to the Google cloud career  readiness program Google cloud has  developed a cloud engineer career  readiness path for students and faculty  in higher education let's take a look at  the cloud landscape and learn more about  the associate cloud engineer track  enterprises are migrating to the cloud  and building new applications on the  cloud leading industry research  indicates that a shift to cloud will  affect more than one trillion dollars in  IT spending adoption of cloud native  applications will double by 2020 this  accelerated move towards cloud has  created a tremendous demand for  qualified professionals who are  proficient in cloud technologies  traditional roles are evolving in a  cloud first world for example an app  developer or data analyst needs new  skills to succeed with cloud  technologies new roles related to DevOps  data science and machine learning are  emerging you can kick start your career  in cloud related career paths  Google's leading-edge Enterprise ready  curriculum and learning resources can  help you achieve industry recognized  associate cloud engineer certification  the associate cloud engineer track  provides training free of charge to  prepare for the associate cloud engineer  certification exam this track includes  access to the architecting with Google  cloud platform specialization on  Coursera this on-demand training  includes six in-depth courses with  videos hands-on labs and quizzes  hands-on experience is crucial for  success with the associate cloud  engineer certification exam you'll  receive credits to complete self-paced  labs on the quick labs platform free of  charge this training puts you on the  path to success for achieving the  associate cloud engineer certification  based on course completion timelines and  other criteria  receive a 50% discount on the  certification exam familiarity with the  following topics is helpful for success  with the associate cloud engineer track  operating systems file systems the IP  networking stack how web browsers and  web servers communicate databases  programming working with Linux at the  command-line and editing text files from  the Linux command line to participate in  this track you'll need a laptop or  desktop with the latest versions of any  popular web browser the Google Chrome  browser is recommended robust internet  connection to access Google cloud  platform console is required let's look  at the training in a bit more detail the  associate cloud engineer track has two  main training components the  architecting with Google cloud platform  specialization on Coursera covers topics  related to exploring and deploying  solution elements including  infrastructure components such as  networks systems and application  services the cloud architecture quest on  the quick labs platform is a set of  hands-on labs that provide practice on  topics and services that appear in the  associate cloud engineer certification  exam it's highly recommended that you  complete additional labs as well the  training you receive in the associate  cloud engineer track provides a solid  foundation for preparing to take this  certification exam however the training  does not teach exactly what you will  need to pass a test practical hands-on  experience is also needed make sure to  get hands-on experience by practicing  with the suggested labs and quick labs  and to review product documentation  you'll learn a course completion  certificate from Google cloud upon  completing the Coursera specialization  successfully success in the Associate  cloud engineer certification exam  enables you to them  straight to potential employers that you  have the skills necessary to succeed in  roles that require proficiency in cloud  technologies the associate cloud  engineer track must be completed in 16  weeks this slide shows a suggested  timeline complete architecting with  Google cloud platform specialization  within the first nine weeks complete  cloud architecture quest and other  hands-on labs by week 16 your access to  Coursera will expire at the end of 16  weeks practice for the certification  exam and complete the exam before the  voucher expiration date remember you can  race ahead of the suggested timeline  let's now take a quick look at the  Student Resource Center the Student  Resource Center includes FA cues as well  as study jam materials for extra  practice to clarify study jams are  essentially workshops if you're not able  to meet other students in a workshop  setting you can work through the study  jam materials on your own as well if you  have questions about the associate cloud  engineer track check the FAQ and the  support section for information happy  learning
 

